


(Ollama/Mistral ↔ OpenAI API)

Flow:

User ----> OpenAI API -----> Mistral LLM-----> back to User.

Meaning:

This diagram shows a specific scenario where a local LLM (like Ollama/Mistral) interacts with OpenAI API.

The user request goes first to OpenAI’s cloud API.

Then the response is handed over to the local model (or vice versa depending on setup).

It’s more of a hybrid workflow: local + external API.

 Use Case: Running Ollama locally but fetching advanced completions/data from OpenAI API.
 Focus: Specific connection between one local model and OpenAI API.
